# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# checkouts to CRLF. A shell script with CRLF has a shebang of "#!/bin/sh\r", and
# Linux then looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", which does not
# exist — the container fails to start with an exec error that says nothing about
# line endings.
#
# The entrypoint is the only thing standing between a deploy and a running
# service, so it is pinned explicitly rather than left to client configuration.
*.sh text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# LightGBM model files are parsed byte-for-byte by the native library on Linux.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git rewrites these to CRLF on
# checkout, and LightGBM's parser then fails with "Model format error, expect a
# tree here" and calls abort() - which does not raise a Python exception, it takes
# the whole uvicorn process down with a core dump. The API returns nothing at all
# and the container restarts. Marking them -text pins the bytes on every platform.
backend/config/models/*.txt -text

# The SQLite store and its journals are binary; never touch them.
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary
